          "original_text": "      business_logic: '- Build job_applications: - Join job to job_application to application; include only applications where applied_at is populated. - Group by job_id, job_title, job_status, job_created_at, and applied_at year and quarter (quarter 1–4). - Compute: - total_applications: count of application rows. - unique_candidates: count of distinct candidate_id. - hired_count: count of applications with status \"hired\". - active_count: count of applications with status \"active\". - rejected_count: count of applications with a rejection timestamp present. - avg_process_days: average days from applied_at to rejected_at if present, otherwise to last_activity_at; exclude non-computable durations; no rounding. - Build interview_metrics: - From job_application joined to application (applied_at populated), left join scheduled_interview and scorecard. - Group by job_id and applied_at year and quarter. - Compute: - total_interviews: distinct count of scheduled_interview_id. - completed_interviews: count of scheduled interviews with status \"completed\" (not distinct). - total_scorecards: distinct count of scorecard_id. - avg_interview_score: average of mapped recommendations across scorecards (strong_yes=4, yes=3, no=2, definitely_not=1); exclude other values and nulls; no rounding. - Join metrics: - Left join interview_metrics to job_applications on job_id, application_year, and application_quarter. - If interview_metrics is missing, set total_interviews, completed_interviews, and total_scorecards to 0; keep avg_interview_score as NULL. - Derive rates (percentages 0–100, double precision, no rounding): - hire_rate: hired_count divided by total_applications times 100; return 0 if the denominator is 0. - interview_rate: total_interviews divided by total_applications times 100; return 0 if the denominator is 0. - interview_to_hire_rate: hired_count divided by total_interviews times 100; return 0 if the denominator is 0. - interview_completion_rate: completed_interviews divided by total_interviews times 100; return 0 if the denominator is 0. - Assign performance_tier (first matching rule applies): - \"Excellent\" if hired_count >= 3 and hire_rate >= 20. - \"Good\" if hired_count >= 2 and hire_rate >= 15. - \"Average\" if hired_count >= 1 and hire_rate >= 10. - \"Needs Improvement\" if total_applications >= 10. - Else \"Low Activity\". - Flags: - is_fast_process: 1 if avg_process_days <= 30 else 0; NULL avg_process_days yields 0. - has_good_interview_quality: 1 if avg_interview_score >= 3.0 else 0; NULL avg_interview_score yields 0. - Final filter and ordering: - Keep only rows where total_applications >= 1. - Order rows by application_year descending, application_quarter descending, then hire_rate descending.'\n",
          "association": "同一原文行同时提及列名和 precision/rounding/format/type-conversion 关键词；未判定语句适用范围"
        }
